// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row derived_impl_invisible_in_impl_block_refused (tier 3, `refuses`). Feature-interaction audit 2026-09-26, cluster derived-impls-invisible-in-impl-blocks: impl-method bodies are checked before the derive-generated impls exist, so a derived method is unknown inside the type's own impl block
// Logos: error [fn Pt__dup]: method call: 'Pt' has no method 'clone' (the same call in main resolves)
// rustc: #[derive(Clone)] + `impl Pt { fn dup(&self) -> Pt { self.clone() } }` compiles and runs, exit 0. Reproduced.
// corpus: tests/interactions/clusters/derived-impls-invisible-in-impl-blocks/
// fix hint: metaprog ordering: run derive expansion (and register the generated impls) before sema checks any impl-method body; not the derive_clone_nonprimitive_field_refused defect (all fields here are i64).
package derived_impl_invisible_in_impl_block_refused;
use logos.std.compiler.metaprog;
use logos.lang.clone;
#[derive_clone]
struct Pt { x: i64, y: i64 }
impl Pt { fn dup(&self) -> Pt { self.clone() } }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let p = Pt { x: 1, y: 2 };
    if p.dup().y != 2 { return 3; }
    return 0;
}
